{"name": "client-cert-csr-create-procA", "kind": "positive", "why": "Procedure A's own write: a create of a certificatesigningrequests object whose requestObject.spec.signerName is kubernetes.io/kube-apiserver-client is the create leg of the chokepoint; the server injects spec.username from the requester (v1.36.4 strategy.go PrepareForCreate), so the minted credential's identity is not spoofable.", "source": "real: recorded on the local kube-apiserver v1.36.4 lab (kubectl create -f a kubernetes.io/kube-apiserver-client CSR, name trr9035-ordinary), logged at Request by the TRR9035 audit-policy row; identity/sourceIP/userAgent normalised to the kind cluster shape (the rule reads neither).", "events": [{"kind": "Event", "apiVersion": "audit.k8s.io/v1", "level": "Request", "auditID": "4bf99233-4289-4222-9b9c-60d95b14f101", "stage": "ResponseComplete", "requestURI": "/apis/certificates.k8s.io/v1/certificatesigningrequests?fieldManager=kubectl-create&fieldValidation=Strict", "verb": "create", "user": {"username": "kubernetes-admin", "groups": ["kubeadm:cluster-admins", "system:authenticated"]}, "sourceIPs": ["172.18.0.1"], "userAgent": "kubectl/v1.36.4 (linux/amd64) kubernetes/bb826b1", "objectRef": {"resource": "certificatesigningrequests", "name": "trr9035-ordinary", "apiGroup": "certificates.k8s.io", "apiVersion": "v1"}, "responseStatus": {"metadata": {}, "code": 201}, "requestObject": {"kind": "CertificateSigningRequest", "apiVersion": "certificates.k8s.io/v1", "metadata": {"name": "trr9035-ordinary"}, "spec": {"request": "", "signerName": "kubernetes.io/kube-apiserver-client", "usages": ["client auth"]}, "status": {}}, "requestReceivedTimestamp": "2026-11-02T00:34:48.073634Z", "stageTimestamp": "2026-11-02T00:34:48.080926Z", "annotations": {"authorization.k8s.io/decision": "allow", "authorization.k8s.io/reason": ""}}]}
{"name": "client-cert-csr-approve-procB", "kind": "positive", "why": "Procedure B's own write: an update of the certificatesigningrequests/approval subresource by a non-system identity is the approve leg of the chokepoint. Here the approver (user.username) is the same identity recorded as the requester (spec.username) on the create above, so this record is in fact a SELF-APPROVAL; the rule fires on it as a generic non-system approval but does NOT verify approver==requester (a Sigma field reference, non-portable -- RULE_DEFECTS.md KTBD-O1 limit 2). The approval update is logged at Metadata, so no signerName is present on this leg.", "source": "real: recorded on the local kube-apiserver v1.36.4 lab (kubectl certificate approve trr9035-ordinary), logged at Metadata by the TRR9035 approval audit-policy row; identity/sourceIP/userAgent normalised to the kind cluster shape.", "events": [{"kind": "Event", "apiVersion": "audit.k8s.io/v1", "level": "Metadata", "auditID": "3b99ec3b-2496-400e-806a-c63ea84f9b4e", "stage": "ResponseComplete", "requestURI": "/apis/certificates.k8s.io/v1/certificatesigningrequests/trr9035-ordinary/approval", "verb": "update", "user": {"username": "kubernetes-admin", "groups": ["kubeadm:cluster-admins", "system:authenticated"]}, "sourceIPs": ["172.18.0.1"], "userAgent": "kubectl/v1.36.4 (linux/amd64) kubernetes/bb826b1", "objectRef": {"resource": "certificatesigningrequests", "name": "trr9035-ordinary", "uid": "43bba80d-1522-48f8-a588-5c05ae7364bd", "apiGroup": "certificates.k8s.io", "apiVersion": "v1", "resourceVersion": "213", "subresource": "approval"}, "responseStatus": {"metadata": {}, "code": 200}, "requestReceivedTimestamp": "2026-11-02T00:34:48.159102Z", "stageTimestamp": "2026-11-02T00:34:48.162171Z", "annotations": {"authorization.k8s.io/decision": "allow", "authorization.k8s.io/reason": ""}}]}
{"name": "node-client-kubelet-csr-near-miss", "kind": "near-miss", "why": "The hard benign baseline for the create leg: a node bootstrap CSR with signerName kubernetes.io/kube-apiserver-client-kubelet (the kubelet authenticating to the API server). It shares the create chokepoint (certificatesigningrequests create in certificates.k8s.io) and differs only on signerName (and a system:node requester, which the rule does not read); flipping signerName to kubernetes.io/kube-apiserver-client alone fires the create leg.", "source": "real: recorded on the local kube-apiserver v1.36.4 lab (a kubernetes.io/kube-apiserver-client-kubelet CSR create); signerName constant from v1.36.4 staging/src/k8s.io/api/certificates/v1/types.go; requester set to a system:node identity to model the node-bootstrap actor.", "breaks": ["select_create.requestObject.spec.signerName"], "events": [{"kind": "Event", "apiVersion": "audit.k8s.io/v1", "level": "Request", "auditID": "bacdf3af-6bc2-4e8e-9ea1-a119a35bc1f8", "stage": "ResponseComplete", "requestURI": "/apis/certificates.k8s.io/v1/certificatesigningrequests?fieldManager=kubectl-create&fieldValidation=Strict", "verb": "create", "user": {"username": "system:node:trr9035-node", "groups": ["system:nodes", "system:authenticated"]}, "sourceIPs": ["172.18.0.1"], "userAgent": "kubectl/v1.36.4 (linux/amd64) kubernetes/bb826b1", "objectRef": {"resource": "certificatesigningrequests", "name": "trr9035-node-client", "apiGroup": "certificates.k8s.io", "apiVersion": "v1"}, "responseStatus": {"metadata": {}, "code": 201}, "requestObject": {"kind": "CertificateSigningRequest", "apiVersion": "certificates.k8s.io/v1", "metadata": {"name": "trr9035-node-client"}, "spec": {"request": "", "signerName": "kubernetes.io/kube-apiserver-client-kubelet", "usages": ["client auth"]}, "status": {}}, "requestReceivedTimestamp": "2026-11-02T00:34:46.502805Z", "stageTimestamp": "2026-11-02T00:34:46.602209Z", "annotations": {"authorization.k8s.io/decision": "allow", "authorization.k8s.io/reason": ""}}]}
{"name": "kubelet-serving-csr-near-miss", "kind": "near-miss", "why": "The second benign node signer: a kubelet-serving CSR (signerName kubernetes.io/kubelet-serving), the TLS serving certificate a kubelet presents. It shares the create chokepoint and differs only on signerName; flipping signerName to kubernetes.io/kube-apiserver-client alone fires the create leg. Together with the client-kubelet near-miss this covers every built-in node signer the create leg must exclude.", "source": "real: recorded on the local kube-apiserver v1.36.4 lab (a kubernetes.io/kubelet-serving CSR create); signerName constant from v1.36.4 certificates/v1/types.go; requester set to a system:node identity.", "breaks": ["select_create.requestObject.spec.signerName"], "events": [{"kind": "Event", "apiVersion": "audit.k8s.io/v1", "level": "Request", "auditID": "76264737-56c9-4b88-b89e-eb3e3405d845", "stage": "ResponseComplete", "requestURI": "/apis/certificates.k8s.io/v1/certificatesigningrequests?fieldManager=kubectl-create&fieldValidation=Strict", "verb": "create", "user": {"username": "system:node:trr9035-node", "groups": ["system:nodes", "system:authenticated"]}, "sourceIPs": ["172.18.0.1"], "userAgent": "kubectl/v1.36.4 (linux/amd64) kubernetes/bb826b1", "objectRef": {"resource": "certificatesigningrequests", "name": "trr9035-node-serving", "apiGroup": "certificates.k8s.io", "apiVersion": "v1"}, "responseStatus": {"metadata": {}, "code": 201}, "requestObject": {"kind": "CertificateSigningRequest", "apiVersion": "certificates.k8s.io/v1", "metadata": {"name": "trr9035-node-serving"}, "spec": {"request": "", "signerName": "kubernetes.io/kubelet-serving", "usages": ["server auth", "digital signature", "key encipherment"]}, "status": {}}, "requestReceivedTimestamp": "2026-11-02T00:34:47.276328Z", "stageTimestamp": "2026-11-02T00:34:47.387114Z", "annotations": {"authorization.k8s.io/decision": "allow", "authorization.k8s.io/reason": ""}}]}
{"name": "csrapprover-auto-approval-filtered", "kind": "filtered", "why": "The benign baseline for the approve leg: the built-in csrapprover controller (system:kube-controller-manager) auto-approving a node CSR by writing the approval subresource. It holds every approve-leg selection item (approval subresource update of a CSR) and is suppressed only by filter_system_approver (user.username begins with 'system:'). Removing that filter would fire the rule on it, so the filter is live, not dead code.", "source": "real: recorded on the local kube-apiserver v1.36.4 lab (the approval record), with the approver set to system:kube-controller-manager to model the built-in csrapprover's auto-approval of node CSRs (kubernetes v1.36.4 cmd/kube-controller-manager, csrapproving controller).", "breaks": ["filter_system_approver.user.username"], "events": [{"kind": "Event", "apiVersion": "audit.k8s.io/v1", "level": "Metadata", "auditID": "3b99ec3b-2496-400e-806a-c63ea84f9b4e", "stage": "ResponseComplete", "requestURI": "/apis/certificates.k8s.io/v1/certificatesigningrequests/trr9035-node-client/approval", "verb": "update", "user": {"username": "system:kube-controller-manager", "groups": ["system:authenticated"]}, "sourceIPs": ["172.18.0.1"], "userAgent": "kubectl/v1.36.4 (linux/amd64) kubernetes/bb826b1", "objectRef": {"resource": "certificatesigningrequests", "name": "trr9035-node-client", "uid": "43bba80d-1522-48f8-a588-5c05ae7364bd", "apiGroup": "certificates.k8s.io", "apiVersion": "v1", "resourceVersion": "213", "subresource": "approval"}, "responseStatus": {"metadata": {}, "code": 200}, "requestReceivedTimestamp": "2026-11-02T00:34:48.159102Z", "stageTimestamp": "2026-11-02T00:34:48.162171Z", "annotations": {"authorization.k8s.io/decision": "allow", "authorization.k8s.io/reason": ""}}]}
{"name": "csr-status-update-near-miss", "kind": "near-miss", "why": "A legitimate look-alike that shares the approve-leg surface but is the status subresource, not approval: an update of certificatesigningrequests/status (where the signer controller writes the issued certificate). It shares the approve leg (certificatesigningrequests update in certificates.k8s.io by a non-system user) and breaks only objectRef.subresource; flipping it to 'approval' alone fires. This proves the approve leg is scoped to the approval decision, not to any CSR subresource write.", "source": "synthetic: modeled on the real approval record with the subresource changed to 'status' (the subresource the signer controller writes the issued cert through).", "breaks": ["select_approval.objectRef.subresource"], "events": [{"kind": "Event", "apiVersion": "audit.k8s.io/v1", "level": "Metadata", "auditID": "3b99ec3b-2496-400e-806a-c63ea84f9b4e", "stage": "ResponseComplete", "requestURI": "/apis/certificates.k8s.io/v1/certificatesigningrequests/trr9035-ordinary/status", "verb": "update", "user": {"username": "kubernetes-admin", "groups": ["kubeadm:cluster-admins", "system:authenticated"]}, "sourceIPs": ["172.18.0.1"], "userAgent": "kubectl/v1.36.4 (linux/amd64) kubernetes/bb826b1", "objectRef": {"resource": "certificatesigningrequests", "name": "trr9035-ordinary", "uid": "43bba80d-1522-48f8-a588-5c05ae7364bd", "apiGroup": "certificates.k8s.io", "apiVersion": "v1", "resourceVersion": "213", "subresource": "status"}, "responseStatus": {"metadata": {}, "code": 200}, "requestReceivedTimestamp": "2026-11-02T00:34:48.159102Z", "stageTimestamp": "2026-11-02T00:34:48.162171Z", "annotations": {"authorization.k8s.io/decision": "allow", "authorization.k8s.io/reason": ""}}]}
{"name": "csr-approval-get-near-miss", "kind": "near-miss", "why": "Reading the approval subresource (verb get) rather than writing it: it shares the approve-leg surface (the approval subresource of a CSR in certificates.k8s.io by a non-system user) and breaks only the verb; flipping get to update alone fires. This proves the approve leg requires a write of the approval decision, not a read of its status.", "source": "synthetic: modeled on the real approval record with the verb changed to 'get' (a read of the approval subresource).", "breaks": ["select_approval.verb"], "events": [{"kind": "Event", "apiVersion": "audit.k8s.io/v1", "level": "Metadata", "auditID": "3b99ec3b-2496-400e-806a-c63ea84f9b4e", "stage": "ResponseComplete", "requestURI": "/apis/certificates.k8s.io/v1/certificatesigningrequests/trr9035-ordinary/approval", "verb": "get", "user": {"username": "kubernetes-admin", "groups": ["kubeadm:cluster-admins", "system:authenticated"]}, "sourceIPs": ["172.18.0.1"], "userAgent": "kubectl/v1.36.4 (linux/amd64) kubernetes/bb826b1", "objectRef": {"resource": "certificatesigningrequests", "name": "trr9035-ordinary", "uid": "43bba80d-1522-48f8-a588-5c05ae7364bd", "apiGroup": "certificates.k8s.io", "apiVersion": "v1", "resourceVersion": "213", "subresource": "approval"}, "responseStatus": {"metadata": {}, "code": 200}, "requestReceivedTimestamp": "2026-11-02T00:34:48.159102Z", "stageTimestamp": "2026-11-02T00:34:48.162171Z", "annotations": {"authorization.k8s.io/decision": "allow", "authorization.k8s.io/reason": ""}}]}
{"name": "csr-get-benign", "kind": "benign", "why": "Ordinary activity: a non-system user reading a CSR (verb get). It must not fire: the create leg needs verb create and a signerName, and the approve leg needs an update of the approval subresource.", "source": "real: recorded on the local kube-apiserver v1.36.4 lab (kubectl get csr), logged at Metadata; identity normalised to the kind shape.", "events": [{"kind": "Event", "apiVersion": "audit.k8s.io/v1", "level": "Metadata", "auditID": "7a8ee3e1-4ccf-4ead-8d6e-1dcd8844b4ef", "stage": "ResponseComplete", "requestURI": "/apis/certificates.k8s.io/v1/certificatesigningrequests/trr9035-ordinary", "verb": "get", "user": {"username": "kubernetes-admin", "groups": ["kubeadm:cluster-admins", "system:authenticated"]}, "sourceIPs": ["172.18.0.1"], "userAgent": "kubectl/v1.36.4 (linux/amd64) kubernetes/bb826b1", "objectRef": {"resource": "certificatesigningrequests", "name": "trr9035-ordinary", "apiGroup": "certificates.k8s.io", "apiVersion": "v1"}, "responseStatus": {"metadata": {}, "code": 200}, "requestReceivedTimestamp": "2026-11-02T00:34:48.154274Z", "stageTimestamp": "2026-11-02T00:34:48.155363Z", "annotations": {"authorization.k8s.io/decision": "allow", "authorization.k8s.io/reason": ""}}]}
